Perfect! I found the file. The answer is:

**`gson/src/main/java/com/google/gson/internal/bind/EnumTypeAdapter.java`**

This is the single file that builds the enum name-to-constant lookup (`nameToConstant` map) used during enum deserialization. 

The relevant code is in the constructor (lines 95-101):

```java
SerializedName annotation = constantField.getAnnotation(SerializedName.class);
if (annotation != null) {
  name = annotation.value();
  for (String alternate : annotation.alternate()) {
    nameToConstant.put(alternate, constant);
  }
}
nameToConstant.put(name, constant);
```

And the lookup is performed in the `read()` method at line 120:
```java
T constant = nameToConstant.get(key);
```

The bug appears to be in how the `nameToConstant` map is populated when `@SerializedName` is present — specifically in lines 95-101 where alternates are being added to the map.
